\begin{csabstract}
Polymarket prices on tennis matches are win probabilities, and each point moves them by an amount we can compute. In
public data on << V('univ.matches') >> matches, the wallets that trade within 3\,s of a point earn after fees in every
month, in and out of sample, while everyone else loses. Copying them at their own prices has a Sharpe ratio of
<< V('v2.is.sr') >> in sample and << V('v2.oos.sr') >> out of sample but loses once fees double. A computer-vision
trader, simulated with an assumed video delay (we did not buy a feed), makes << V('sc.pre.oos.v1.usd') >> a day out of sample at 1\,s pre-registered (<< V('sc.cal.oos.v1.usd') >> post hoc); a
replay on real order books loses.

