We use every resolved ATP, WTA and Challenger singles match market on Polymarket with at least
<< V('univ.minvol') >> traded, << V('univ.first') >> to << V('univ.last') >>: << V('univ.matches') >> matches and
<< V('univ.volume') >> of volume, from public order books and trade tapes \citep{pmapi}. \emph{In sample} (IS) is the
first 80\% of matches by start time; \emph{out of sample} (OOS) is the last << V('univ.oos') >>, from
<< V('univ.oosstart') >> (the last << V('univ.oos_time') >> by time). We looked at the OOS while building v2 and the
CV simulation, so it is \emph{burned}. For a blind test, which also checks survivorship, we held back
<< V('u2.markets') >> smaller markets we never examined and opened them once per frozen rule. Six tapes hit the API's
offset cap, << V('data.nofee') >> early matches paid no fee, << V('data.res5050') >> of markets settled 50/50 (kept),
tape timestamps run << V('data.blocklag') >>\,s late, and no corporate actions apply. Timing data: ESPN and the WTA
\citep{espn,wtaapi}; vision: OpenTTGames footage \citep{voeikov2020}, BlurBall and WASB weights
