\para{Costs and validation} Polymarket charges takers \(f(q) = r\,q\,(1-q)\) a share at price \(q\), which is
\(10{,}000\,r\,(1-q)\) bps of notional. Today \(r = << V('fee.rate') >>\), so a trade at 50¢ pays
<< V('calc.fee.q50.c') >>¢ a share (<< V('fee.bps_q05') >>\,bps). Each match pays its actual fee and every trade the spread
it crossed; we also double both. v2 paid << V('v2.is.fee_bps') >> and
<< V('v2.oos.fee_bps') >>\,bps of notional in fees (IS, OOS) and still netted << V('v2.is.net_bps') >> and
<< V('v2.oos.net_bps') >>\,bps. We tune only in sample, walk-forward (fit on past months, test on the next).

