figures (C) and the records (D). Each value is in \texttt{results/paper/numbers.json} with its source file.

\para{A1. Sharpe ratio} \(\text{SR} = \sqrt{365}\,\bar d / s_d\), where \(d_t\) is net P\&L on every calendar day
(zero on days without trades) and \(s_d\) its standard deviation. v2 IS: \(\bar d = << V('calc.is.mean') >>\),
\(s_d = << V('calc.is.sd') >>\) over \(T = << V('calc.is.T') >>\) days, so the daily ratio is << V('calc.is.srd') >>
and \(\text{SR} = << V('calc.is.srd') >> \times << V('calc.sqrt365') >> = << V('calc.is.sr') >>\). OOS:
\(<< V('calc.oos.mean') >> / << V('calc.oos.sd') >> \times << V('calc.sqrt365') >> = << V('calc.oos.sr') >>\).

\para{A2. Sortino ratio} \(\sqrt{365}\,\bar d / \text{DD}\), where the downside deviation is \(\text{DD} =
\sqrt{\tfrac1T\sum_t \min(d_t,0)^2}\). For v2 OOS, \(\text{DD} = << V('calc.so.dd') >>\), so the ratio is
\(\sqrt{365}\times << V('calc.oos.mean') >> / << V('calc.so.dd') >> = << V('calc.so') >>\).

\para{A3. Maximum drawdown} \(\text{MDD} = \min_t \big(E_t - \max_{s\le t} E_s\big)\), where \(E_t\) is cumulative
P\&L, as a share of capital. v2 OOS: \(<< V('calc.mdd') >> / << V('calc.oos.cap') >> = << V('calc.mdd.pct') >>\).

\para{A4. Probabilistic Sharpe} The chance that the true daily Sharpe beats \(\text{SR}^*\), given the sample length
\(T\), skew \(\gamma_3\) and kurtosis \(\gamma_4\) \citep{bailey2014}:
\[\text{PSR}(\text{SR}^*) = \Phi\Big((\widehat{\text{SR}}-\text{SR}^*)\sqrt{T-1}\,\Big/\sqrt{1-\gamma_3\widehat{\text{SR}}+\tfrac{\gamma_4-1}{4}\widehat{\text{SR}}^2}\Big).\]
v2 OOS: \(\widehat{\text{SR}} = << V('calc.oos.srd') >>\), \(T = << V('calc.oos.T') >>\),
\(\gamma_3 = << V('calc.oos.skew') >>\), \(\gamma_4 = << V('calc.oos.kurt') >>\), so \(\text{PSR}(0) = << V('calc.psr0') >>\).

\para{A5. Deflated Sharpe} \(\text{DSR} = \text{PSR}(\text{SR}_0)\), where \(\text{SR}_0\) is the best Sharpe we would
expect from \(N\) tries on pure noise, with \(\gamma\) the Euler--Mascheroni constant:
\[\text{SR}_0 = \sqrt{V}\Big((1-\gamma)\,\Phi^{-1}\big(1-\tfrac1N\big) + \gamma\,\Phi^{-1}\big(1-\tfrac{1}{Ne}\big)\Big).\] v2 OOS with \(N =
<< V('rig.N3386') >>\) and \(V = 1/(T-1)\): the two \(\Phi^{-1}\) terms are << V('calc.z1') >> and << V('calc.z2') >>,
\(\text{SR}_0 = << V('calc.sr0d') >>\) a day (<< V('calc.sr0a') >> a year), and DSR \(= << V('calc.dsr') >>\).
Table~\ref{tab:head} shows the lowest DSR over three choices of \(V\).

\para{A6. Probability of backtest overfitting} \citep{bailey2017}. Split the daily P\&L of << V('rig.pbo.n') >>
variants into \(S = << V('rig.pbo.S') >>\) blocks. For each of the \(\binom{16}{8} = << V('rig.pbo.splits') >>\) ways
to call half the blocks in sample, take the best in-sample variant, find its rank \(\omega\) out of sample and set
\(\lambda = \ln\frac{\omega}{1-\omega}\); PBO \(= \Pr(\lambda \le 0)\). v2-safe grid: PBO \(= << V('rig.pbo.lowloss') >>\)
(median \(\lambda = << V('rig.pbo.logit_med') >>\)).

\para{A7. Stationary block bootstrap} \citep{politis1994}. Resample days in blocks of random length (mean 5 days)
10,000 times and read the percentiles. v2 OOS Sharpe: << V('v2.oos.sr_ci') >>, standard error << V('calc.boot.se') >>,
\(P(\text{SR}\le 0) = << V('rig.boot.p') >>\).

\para{A8. Factor regression} \(r_t = \alpha + \beta_M\,\text{MktRF}_t + \beta_S\,\text{SMB}_t + \beta_H\,\text{HML}_t
+ \beta_U\,\text{Mom}_t + \varepsilon_t\) on daily return on capital, with Newey--West errors (5 lags)
\citep{fama1993,carhart1997,newey1987,french}. v2 IS (<< V('fac.n') >> days): \(\alpha = << V('calc.ff.alpha') >>\) a day
(\(t = << V('fac.alpha_t') >>\)); \(\beta_M = << V('calc.ff.MktRF') >>\) (\(t = << V('calc.ff.MktRF.t') >>\)),
\(\beta_S = << V('calc.ff.SMB') >>\), \(\beta_H = << V('calc.ff.HML') >>\), \(\beta_U = << V('calc.ff.Mom') >>\);
\(R^2 = << V('fac.r2') >>\).

\para{A9. Taker fee} \(f(q) = r\,q(1-q)\) a share at price \(q\), or \(r(1-q)\) per dollar, which is
\(10{,}000\,r(1-q)\) bps. At \(r = << V('fee.rate') >>\): \(q = 0.5\) pays << V('calc.fee.q50.c') >>¢
(<< V('calc.fee.q50.bps') >>\,bps) and \(q = 0.8\) pays << V('calc.fee.q80.c') >>¢ (<< V('calc.fee.q80.bps') >>\,bps).

\para{A10. Point swing} \(\Delta(k)\) of Section~\ref{sec:hyp}, with the match-win probability computed exactly by recursion over points,
games, tiebreaks and sets (\texttt{src/markov.py}). Two equal players who win << V('calc.mk.ps') >> of service points:
at the first point \(\Pr(\text{win}) = << V('calc.mk.start.p') >>\), moving to << V('calc.mk.start.up') >> or
<< V('calc.mk.start.dn') >>, so \(\Delta = << V('calc.mk.start.lev') >>\). Serving at 5--5, 30--40 in the deciding
set, \(\Pr(\text{win}) = << V('calc.mk.bp.p') >>\), moving to << V('calc.mk.bp.up') >> or << V('calc.mk.bp.dn') >>, so
\(\Delta = << V('calc.mk.bp.lev') >>\). The mean \(|\Delta|\) over a match is << V('markov.lev') >>.

\para{A11. Latency budget} Eq.~\ref{eq:budget}. With the pre-registered \(L = << V('cv.pre.lag') >>\)\,s, \(D =
<< V('venue.delay') >>\)\,s and our measured \(\delta = << V('e2e.delta_s') >>\)\,s, a point whose book reprices at the
median \(R = << V('lat.book_vs_stamp_signed') >>\)\,s needs \(V < << V('calc.vmax.med') >> + \ell\): no feed wins it
without an early call. At the 90th percentile, \(R = << V('calc.R.p90') >>\)\,s and \(V < << V('calc.vmax.p90') >>\)\,s.
The sweep's break-even (<< V('cv.pre.be.is') >>\,s IS) comes from these late reprices.

\para{A12. Capital and return on capital} Capital is three times the peak dollars locked in open positions,
each held 4\,h or until resolution. v2 IS: peak << V('calc.peak') >>, capital << V('v2.is.cap') >>; return \(= 365\,\bar
d/\text{capital} = 365 \times << V('calc.is.mean') >> / << V('v2.is.cap') >> = << V('calc.roc') >>\) a year.

\para{A13. Capacity and volume share} Capacity is the capital at which the seed-mean Sharpe falls to half its
smallest-size value; share is our notional a day over market volume a day. CV, post hoc, IS, just below half Sharpe:
<< V('capcv.notional') >> a day against << V('cap.inplay') >> of in-play volume (<< V('capcv.share_inplay') >>) and
<< V('cap.fastq') >> traded by the fast tier 0--3\,s after a point (<< V('capcv.share_fast') >>).

